<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Roger-Bernard III of Foix</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1243–1302</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Roger-Bernard III was Count of Foix from 1265 to 1302 and, through marriage, Viscount of Castelbon. He clashed at times with the kings of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and Aragon, was imprisoned by both, and was also known as a troubadour poet. In 1278 he signed the first Pareatge with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">Bishop</a> of Urgell, creating the joint lordship of Andorra that his heirs, and later the French head of state, inherited.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/roger-bernard-iii-of-foix.jpg" alt="Roger-Bernard III of Foix" width="287" height="257" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Germain Demay · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Roger1276.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
